[step 1] $ W=$(mktemp -d) && WORK="$W/example" && echo "WORK=$WORK"
WORK=/tmp/tmp.3Tsmlu5bti/example
expected: a new directory
got:      /tmp/tmp.3Tsmlu5bti
All output of this run also goes to /tmp/tmp.3Tsmlu5bti/quickstart-gpu.log.
From here on HOME and TMPDIR are /tmp/tmp.3Tsmlu5bti.

quickstart-gpu needs: one NVIDIA H100 that nothing else uses, and its driver;
CUDA 13.2 Update 2 (nvcc 13.2.86); the driver's library
registered with the system's loader, and the toolkit's libraries registered too or in its
directory lib64 or lib, if that meets the conditions in prover/docs/build.md; gcc and g++ 13;
python3, binutils and flock; an x86-64 CPU with the SHA extensions; 10 GB of available
memory; 1 GB of free disk space in the repository and 2 GB in /tmp, both on a local disk.
It checks for each of these first, except for those conditions, which the second build checks.
It writes to bin/ and prover/build/ in the repository and to /tmp/tmp.3Tsmlu5bti.
The whole run takes about half an hour, nearly all of it the second build.

[step 2] $ nvidia-smi --id=0 --query-gpu=name,compute_cap,driver_version,memory.used --format=csv,noheader,nounits
NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3, 9.0, 595.91.07, 0
expected: a GPU of compute capability 9.0, as an H100 has, with less than 1024 MiB in use
got:      NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3, compute capability 9.0, driver 595.91.07, 0 MiB in use

[step 3] $ type -P nvcc && nvcc --version | tail -n 2; prover/check_nvcc_version.sh
/home/tester/cuda-13.2.86/nvidia/cu13/bin/nvcc
Cuda compilation tools, release 13.2, V13.2.86
Build cuda_13.2.r13.2/compiler.37953736_0
expected: a path, a version, and exit status 0
got:      exit status 0

[step 4] $ gcc -dumpfullversion -dumpversion; g++ -dumpfullversion -dumpversion
13.3.0
13.3.0
expected: gcc and g++, each 13 (tested: 13.3) or later (untested)
got:      gcc 13, g++ 13

