[step 10] $ flock -n "$W" true && flock -n . true
expected: exit status 0: both directories can be locked
got:      exit status 0

A short program that calls the CUDA runtime goes to /tmp/tmp.3Tsmlu5bti/cuda_check.cu.

[step 11] $ nvcc -std=c++17 --gpu-architecture=sm_90a --cudart=static -o "$W/cuda_check" "$W/cuda_check.cu" && "$W/cuda_check"
the CUDA runtime reached the GPU
expected: the CUDA runtime reached the GPU
got:      the CUDA runtime reached the GPU

Next: two builds. The first takes a minute or two. The second takes about half an hour and
prints little but compiler warnings, which are not failures: this script checks each build's
exit status.

[step 12] $ verifier/build.sh
build=93afdaf592393a54ebd17b681d1c03295eb883f0161ff0e6ab872a3b39939595 dw=8
compiling cp_verify.cpp: one compiler call of one to two minutes, which prints nothing while it runs
